The `LICENSE` file (MIT) covers the application source code only. It does
**not** cover map data or any artefact derived from it.

Map data, and everything derived from it, comes from OpenStreetMap and is
licensed under the **Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0**. This notice covers
the following artefacts, when present in this repository or produced from it:

- `data/seed/<slug>/bars.json`
- `data/seed/<slug>/city.geojson`
- `data/seed/<slug>/districts.geojson`
- `data/seed/<slug>/neighbours.geojson`
- `data/seed/<slug>/grid.bin` and `data/seed/<slug>/grid-meta.json`
- the `.pmtiles` tile extract (published as a GitHub Release asset, see
  `SPEC.md` Section 13.2, and reproducible from `scripts/extract-tiles.sh`)

The seed tree is per city — `<slug>` is the city slug, `karlsruhe` today (see
`SPEC.md` Section 11.4). These paths were flat until that seam existed.

Every one of these is committed today except the `.pmtiles` extract, which is
deliberately never committed (`SPEC.md` Section 13.2). This notice applies to
it, and to any further city's seed tree, from the moment it exists.

